I really hope someone can help me with this.  I have installed NT and the
KB works fine as well as installing RH through the SRM (but I can't get it
to boot afterwards since there is no MILO installation during the RH
setup).  I know the KB to system connectivity is fine.

The problem:

When installing using MILO, at the "MILO>" prompt, the keyboard mapping
craps out.  Symptoms?  Typing "j" renders "e", "backspace" renders "`", "m"
renders " " etc etc etc.  No logical order and nothing is mapped correctly.

The system:

UDB flashed to 4.3.3.  96MB, scsi hdd, ext cdrom.  KB is connected via a
Cybex commander box.  (Which works fine with NT and RH install from SRM).

What is going on here?

Are there instructions to install RH from SRM without having to boot the
system off floppy?  I'd appreciate it if someone has them.




