> and deleting th 8 (a-h) partitions, but with no success, because the disk
> is recognized yet as with a BSD disklabel)

For booting from SRM console, you really do want to use BSD disklabels,
unless you like booting from floppy... ;-}

Yes, you may be able to fudge diskdruid/fdisk to create a DOS disklabel
that you can install the bootstrap over, but it is a kludge, IMHO.

As for clearing out an existing disklabel, I find that:

	dd if=/dev/zero of=/dev/sda bs=512 count=2

usually does the trick, as DOS and BSD disklabels are in the first two blocks.

Good luck.

--Jay++

