actually, ttySx hasn't replaced cuax, cause it was always there. It
was supposed to be that ttySx was for incoming, cuax for outgoing,
each port had slightly different ioctl's/behaviour. 

now cuax has been obsoleted, so your only choice is ttySx. (which
might become /dev/tts/x if devfs goes into 2.3)

