Hello Everyone,

I've been trying to use MySQL on Alpha/Linux, however, I've been
encountering odd behavior that doesn't seem to happen on x86. I'm
wondering if anyone else has encountered similar problems.

When connecting to MySQL with the mysql client, running queries work
just fine. However, when I run queries from PHP pages, MySQL starts
eating up memory and freezes. From that point on, the mysql client
cannot connect nor run queries (if already connected). The only way
that I can find to remedy the problem is to kill the mysqld process
and restart it manually.

Note, this is not even under heavy load, which seemed to be a problem
someone previously mentioned. Also, the exact configuration on x86
seems to work without any problems. 

Here is some info:

Linux 2.2.5
MySQL 3.22.20a compiled w/ egcs-1.1.2
PHP 3.0.7
Apache 1.3.6

If anyone has any suggestions, please do! Thanks.
D.

