On 22 Apr 1999, Aidan Williams wrote:

> Greetings,
> ...
>=20
> I have tried passing boot parameters to tell the floppy driver that it=20
> is 1.44mb along the lines of:

You don't need to do this

>=20
>   boot -file vmlinux.gz -flags "floppy=3D0,4,cmos root=3Ddev/fd0 loadramd=
isk=3D1"

The RedHat manual have a typo error. Use instead:
boot dva0 -file vmlinux.gz -fl "root=3D/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=3D1
prompt_ramdisk=3D1"

>...
=20
>=20
> I don't have another alpha/linux system lying around to make an NFS
> root filesystem on.  I also tried the updated ramdisk.img.
>=20
> Anyone successfully done an install like this before?
> Can you do this via tftp or something?
>=20
> regards
> =09aidan

Be sure that the boot and remdisk image files are correct. If you have
dowloaded them via the net, check them; if you are using the CD-ROM, sure
they are ok. Create the disks following the instructions on the RH Manual.

> ...=20
>=20

