Uh-oh... see below.

> At the MILO> prompt, type:
> 
> boot fd0:vmlinux.gz root=3D/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=3D1 prompt_ramdisk=3D1
> 
> When I go to type the 'a' in 'load' it types many 'a's' and won't go any =
> further. I have updated to the latest firmware. I have a 4.3GB external =
> SCSI drive. I have NT (Alpha) installed on two FAT partitions. Any =
> assistance is appreciated. Thanks.

You probably also have a modem on COM1.  MILO echoes to COM1, and
accepts input either from the keyboard or COM1.  When the modem sees
'a' it determines the baud rate, and begins echoing.  MILO echoes, the
modem echoes....

Move the modem to COM2 and this problem should go away.

> ------=_NextPart_000_00D6_01BE8CFF.1B3A0950
> Content-Type: text/html;
> 	charset="iso-8859-1"
> Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Please limit HTML mail to those who you know want to receive it.
It's particularly discourteous on a mailing list where some recipients
have to pay by the minute for their connection time -- redundant HTML
copies of a message cost them money.

