Just out of curiousity:
  How did you get xmp to work correctly on your SB AWE?
Do you use the wavetable engine to play mods?
If yes, did you have to patch xmp to play at correct speed?
I ask because the last time I compiled xmp I had to patch it in order to get
the correct speed. Xmp uses the midi timer ticks to measure time and those
ticks are measured in clock ticks. And on the Alpha the clock ticks at
1024Hz, not at 100Hz like on Intel based machines. There is an IOCTL to read
the timer-ticks per seconds but xmp did not use that :( (not very
portable...)

> The only thing left is a complaint at boottime that synthfm.sbk is not a
> sound font file.
Maybe the file is indeed corrupt. But for xmp this does not matter at all
because it will overwrite those soundfonts with the samples from the mods
you are playing.

