Mark Henry wrote:

> I earlier created a 1.5MB /milo partition as
> suggested in the install guide.

In this partition you want to put linload.exe and use that to boot from ARC.
Make sure it is formatted FAT so that ARC can read it.

This is how it works on the UDB.

If you don't have this file (I think there's two actually, but I can't read my
FAT partition <g>) you should still be able to get it from gatekeeper.dec.com
in the LinuxAlpha directory.

