Near the bottom of those instructions, there was a instruction that read "dd
if=/dev/fd0 of=/dev/sda1" ( or something close to that, I'm flying from
memory, you may experience slight turbulence) you need to do that, then add
a boot entry in AlphaBIOS to point to MILO on
scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(1).  
      
       LOADIDENTIFIER =Linux
       SYSTEMPARTITION=scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(1)
       OSLOADER=scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(1)\linload.exe
       OSLOADERPARTITION=scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(1)   
       OSLOADFILENAME=\milo
       OSLOADOPTIONS=boot sda2:vmlinux.gz

( or something close)


double check the HOW-TO MILO.

