Hi,

I assume you use the AlphaBIOS to load loadlin and
MILO... and then from MILO you are doing something
like:

MILO> boot floppy

??? yes?

If so.. at the MILO prompt do this instead:

MILO> boot sdaX:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sdaX mem="256M"

replace the sdaX with your root partition... the root
and mem options are "optional" ... but I have
encountered problems with detecting all memory in the
past.. so I'm use to passing the mem option.

I hope this helps.

D.

